id: ops-braces-audit
title: Eliminate the unpatched braces dependency while preserving jscpd 4 parity acceptance
description: "Full npm audit reports GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm on braces 3.0.3 via micromatch, fast-glob, @jscpd/finder and the jscpd4 4.3.0 alias. npm latest braces is 3.0.3 and no patched registry release exists. Removing the alias would remove required real-engine parity tests, which is forbidden. Certification ops-hiee stays NOT READY for this independent audit gate."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[2]: dependencies,security
created_at: "2026-10-04T10:51:17.651Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-04T10:51:18.521Z"
author: codex-sol
repro_steps: npm ci; npm audit; npm ls braces; npm view braces version
expected_result: Both npm audit and npm audit --omit=dev return zero vulnerabilities without deleting jscpd4 engine-parity tests or weakening thresholds.
actual_result: "npm audit: 5 high findings in the same unpatched braces chain; npm audit --omit=dev: zero vulnerabilities."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  package.json,project,Required jscpd4 parity dependency
  test/lint-and-duplication-gates.test.ts,project,Real jscpd4 parity tests must remain
